  "transcript": "User: Hi — I saw your ad on Facebook about answering missed calls. I keep losing patients after hours, so I'm curious how it works.\nAgent: Got it—glad the ad caught your eye. After hours, when a patient calls in, does it go straight to voicemail or ring to an answering service?\nUser: After hours, calls go straight to voicemail. We don't have an answering service.\nAgent: Makes sense—when those after-hours calls hit voicemail, do they usually leave a message and call back, or do you think they’re calling another practice?\nUser: I think they're calling another practice. Missed calls often mean lost patients to competitors.\nAgent: Yeah… that’s the brutal part. Has anyone ever showed you the math on what those after-hours missed calls are costing you?\nUser: I haven't seen the exact math, but I know we're losing potential bookings and revenue. Can you explain?\nAgent: Totally—it's basically: missed after-hours calls × the percent who would’ve booked if you answered × your average appointment value, and that gives you the revenue you’re likely missing. \n\nSo ballpark, how many after-hours calls a week do you think are hitting voicemail—10, 20, 30?\nUser: About 20 calls a week hit voicemail, and I believe about half would book if answered.\nAgent: Got it. And what’s your average appointment value—about how much is a typical new patient worth in dollars?\nUser: Our average appointment value is around $650.\nAgent: Got it—at 20 after-hours calls a week, ~50% booking, and $650 each, that’s about **$6,500/week**, or roughly **$28,100/month** in missed revenue.\n\nIt’s a 20-minute walkthrough—Jay will show you exactly how we catch those after-hours calls and what your numbers look like with it on; what’s better for you, later today or tomorrow?\nUser: Let's book the live call for tomorrow. Can you offer me some afternoon slots?\nAgent: Absolutely—before I grab afternoon options for tomorrow, quick check: are you on Central time?\nUser: Yes, I'm on Central time here in Chicago.\nAgent: Perfect—thanks. What’s your first name?\nUser: My first name is Maria.\nAgent: Got it, Maria—what’s your last name?\nUser: My last name is Gonzales.\nAgent: Thanks—what’s the name of your practice?\nUser: My practice is called Bright Smile Dental.\nAgent: Perfect—And is the number you’re calling from the best contact number to reach you for the SMS confirmation?\nUser: No, the best number is +13125551234. Please send the SMS confirmation there.\nAgent: Perfect—I've got tomorrow afternoon openings at **1:00 PM** or **3:15 PM** Central. Which works for you?\nUser: Let's book the live call for 3:15 PM Central tomorrow.\nAgent: Alright, let me lock that in real quick.\nUser: Yes, please book the live call for 3:15 PM Central tomorrow. Thank you!\nAgent: One moment while I confirm that.\nAgent: Thanks, Maria—you're booked for **tomorrow at 3:15 PM Central** with Jay. You’ll receive an **SMS text** at **+1 (312) 555-1234** with the confirmation details—you can add it to your calendar in one click, or reschedule if you need to.\n\nIs there anything else I can help you with?\nUser: Sure, I'll wait. Please let me know once it's confirmed.\nAgent: All set, Maria—it’s confirmed for tomorrow at 3:15 PM Central, and that SMS confirmation will come through to +1 (312) 555-1234 in just a moment. Really glad you called—Jay’s looking forward to it. Have a great rest of your day. Bye!",
